{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.rrl_gluing_at_sqrt_minus_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.rrl_gluing_at_sqrt_minus_seven","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L92-L105","doc":"The three derived edge rows of the R²L bundle, in rect form\n`Π z^a (1−z)^b`: `a = (2,1,1), b = (0,1,1)`; `a = (−2,0,0), b = (2,−2,−2)`;\n`a = (0,−1,−1), b = (−2,1,1)`. At the exact shapes `z₀ = (5+r)/4`, `z₁ = z₂ = (3+r)/4` with\n`r² = −7` the first row equals `1`; the other two are its inverse-type partners and follow from\nthe same identity. Only the first is stated; the probe verifies all three symbolically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.figure_eight_gluing_at_sixth_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.figure_eight_gluing_at_sixth_root","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L78-L84","doc":"**The derived figure-eight edge equation at a primitive sixth root of unity.** If\n`ω² − ω + 1 = 0` then `ω (1 − ω) = 1`, hence `z₀ z₁ (1 − z₀)(1 − z₁) = 1` at `z₀ = z₁ = ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.trefoil_control_trace_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.trefoil_control_trace_one","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L69-L72","doc":"Control: the positive braid `σ₁σ₂σ₁σ₂` (closure the trefoil) has monodromy `T₁ T₂ = R · L⁻¹`\nwith trace `1`, i.e. `Δ = t² − t + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.stallings_charpoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.stallings_charpoly","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L62-L67","doc":"`det(t·1 − φ) = t² − 3t + 1`: the Alexander polynomial of `4₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.stallings_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.stallings_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L59-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.stallings_trace_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.stallings_trace_three","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L56-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.stallings_monodromy_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.stallings_monodromy_eq","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L50-L54","doc":"**Stallings monodromy of `(σ₁σ₂⁻¹)²`.** Column 1 (two positive crossings) contributes\n`T_{γ₁} = R`, column 2 (two negative crossings) contributes `T_{γ₂}⁻¹ = L`; the fibre is their\nMurasugi sum and the monodromy their product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.L","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.L","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L47-L48","doc":"`T_{γ₂}⁻¹` in the same basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.R","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FigureEightGluingFromMonodromy.lean#L44-L45","doc":"Dehn twist `T_{γ₁}` on `H₁(F; ℤ)` in the basis `(γ₁, γ₂)` with `γ₁ · γ₂ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}